Keep QNX's major()/minor() macros away from uni-algo's version class.

QNX's <sys/types.h> defines major(device) and minor(device) as function-
like macros. The bundled uni-algo header has member functions of those
names in its version class, which the preprocessor rewrote into syntax
errors ("expected unqualified-id before 'int'"). The macros are removed
before the class; nothing in libpiper uses device numbers.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/libpiper/include/uni_algo.h
+++ b/libpiper/include/uni_algo.h
@@ -64272,6 +64272,15 @@
 
 namespace una::version {
 
+// <sys/types.h> of some systems (QNX; glibc before 2.28) defines major() and
+// minor() as macros for device numbers.
+#ifdef major
+#undef major
+#endif
+#ifdef minor
+#undef minor
+#endif
+
 class library_v
 {
 private:
